 "_gloss_note": "Shakespeare word meanings for Stage 4. simplify.py adds an entry to the prompt only when its key appears in the raw text of the chunk (whole word, case-insensitive, ’ = '). Keys may be phrases. Fix a recurring misreading by adding or sharpening an entry here, never by editing drafts. Explain single words only; never paraphrase a famous line here (the model will swap the explanation in and lose the line).",
 "gloss": {
  "anon": "'coming!' or 'right away' (a reply to someone calling), or 'soon'",
  "by and by": "in a moment",
  "i come": "I'm coming",
  "within": "(of a voice or noise) from inside, offstage",
  "counsel": "advice (only in the phrase 'stumblest on my counsel' does it mean private thoughts)",
  "stumblest on my counsel": "happen to overhear my private thoughts",
  "bescreen'd": "hidden",
  "wherefore": "why (never 'where')",
  "art": "are (as in 'thou art' = 'you are')",
  "thou art": "you are",
  "wilt": "will",
  "wert": "were",
  "dost": "do",
  "hast": "have",
  "fain": "gladly; would like to",
  "'haviour": "behaviour",
  "light": "(of a woman or love) not serious, too easily won; also: weightless",
  "strange": "distant, reserved, playing hard to get",
  "cunning to be strange": "skill at pretending not to care",
  "fond": "foolish; also: loving too much",
  "owes": "owns, has",
  "doff": "take off, throw away",
  "o'erperch": "fly over",
  "prorogued": "postponed, delayed",
  "wanting": "lacking, without",
  "perjuries": "broken promises, lies under oath",
  "jove": "Jupiter, king of the Roman gods",
  "idolatry": "worship",
